id: F23
target: src/sello/field.nim
desc: feSqrtRatioM1: correction-select condition inverted, 'feCMove(r, rPrime, bool(uint8(flippedSignSqrt) or uint8(flippedSignSqrtI)))' -> 'feCMove(r, rPrime, not bool(uint8(flippedSignSqrt) or uint8(flippedSignSqrtI)))' -- selects the SQRT_M1-corrected candidate exactly when the ORIGINAL candidate already checked out (correctSignSqrt), and keeps the uncorrected candidate exactly when a correction was actually needed. Replaces the retired F21 (its OLD target, field.feSqrtRatioVartime, was deleted by RFC-004 slice 1c) against the CT primitive's own defect class: which candidate feCMove selects on wasSquare. Re-anchored (CT-hazard fix batch): the select combine moved from Nim's short-circuiting bool 'or' to the bitwise 'bool(uint8(a) or uint8(b))' idiom (see feSqrtRatioM1's own doc comment) to close a confirmed branch-in-disassembly finding; the OLD/NEW pair here was updated to match the new source text verbatim while preserving the identical inverted-select defect class, the same re-anchoring register as S07's precedent.
====OLD====
  feCMove(r, rPrime, bool(uint8(flippedSignSqrt) or uint8(flippedSignSqrtI)))
====NEW====
  feCMove(r, rPrime, not bool(uint8(flippedSignSqrt) or uint8(flippedSignSqrtI)))
====END====
